          "id": 6,
          "title": "Implement Permission-Based UI Rendering",
          "description": "Create conditional UI rendering based on user roles and permissions from Microsoft Entra ID",
          "dependencies": [
            5
          ],
          "details": "Develop permission-aware UI components that conditionally render based on user roles, create higher-order components or hooks for permission checks, implement factory-specific UI elements based on manufacturing roles, and ensure UI state reflects current user permissions. Integrate with existing layout components to maintain consistent UI experience.\n<info added on 2025-05-25T00:29:28.413Z>\n# Permission-Based UI Rendering System Implementation\n\n## Implementation Plan\n1. Create enhanced UI components for conditional rendering based on permissions\n2. Develop permission-aware factory-specific UI elements\n3. Integrate permission checks with existing layout components (MESHeader, MESSidebar)\n4. Create manufacturing-specific conditional UI elements\n5. Add permission-based navigation items and menu visibility\n6. Implement role-based form field visibility and interaction controls\n\n## Current Assessment\n- Strong foundation already exists: RoleGuard, PermissionGuard components\n- Authentication context provides comprehensive permission checking methods\n- Layout components (MESHeader, MESSidebar) need permission integration\n- Need to create factory-specific conditional UI elements\n\n## Next Steps\n- Enhance existing guard components with factory-specific features\n- Create permission-aware navigation and layout integration\n- Build manufacturing-specific conditional rendering components\n</info added on 2025-05-25T00:29:28.413Z>\n<info added on 2025-05-25T00:38:01.771Z>\n## Implementation Completed\n\n### Core Permission-Aware Components (/components/ui/permission-aware.tsx):\n- ManufacturingRoleGuard with manufacturing context and fallback options\n- ManufacturingPermissionGuard with detailed feedback and missing permission display\n- ConditionalRender wrapper for conditional UI elements\n- PermissionButton with role/permission checking and fallback states\n- ManufacturingFeatureFlag for manufacturing features based on roles\n- PermissionNavItem for sidebar navigation\n- FactoryStatusIndicator with permission-aware details display\n- RoleAccessIndicator with visual role-based access indicators\n\n### Layout Integration Components (/components/ui/permission-aware-layout.tsx):\n- PermissionAwareSidebar with role-based navigation, equipment status monitoring, and factory status\n- PermissionAwarePageContainer with optional role/permission requirements\n- PermissionAwareDashboardGrid with role-based widget visibility\n\n### Manufacturing-Specific Features:\n- Role-based navigation mapping for MES routes\n- Permission-based equipment monitoring (Mashing01, Fermentation01, Distillation01, CIP System)\n- Role-based factory status visibility for leadership and engineering\n- Full integration with distillery-specific roles (Operations, Engineering & Technology, Maintenance)\n\n### Demo and Testing:\n- Enhanced Auth Demo Page with comprehensive demonstration section\n- Dedicated test page for permission-aware layout components\n- Interactive examples for all permission-based UI components\n- All TypeScript/ESLint errors resolved\n- Components successfully integrated and functioning properly\n- System ready for production use\n</info added on 2025-05-25T00:38:01.771Z>",
          "status": "done",
          "testStrategy": "Test UI rendering with different user roles, verify conditional elements appear/disappear appropriately, and confirm manufacturing-specific UI elements match role requirements"
        }
      ]
