    {
      "id": 8,
      "title": "Develop Recipe Template Library and Search",
      "description": "Create a comprehensive recipe template library with advanced categorization, search, and filtering capabilities to support multiple customers and complex mash bill patterns.",
      "status": "done",
      "dependencies": [
        6
      ],
      "priority": "medium",
      "details": "1. Implement recipe template storage and retrieval\n2. Create categorization system by whiskey types (RyeBourbon, WheatBourbon, etc.)\n3. Implement customer-specific template organization and access control for JBM Liquid Assets, Bernstein-Gruppe AG, Ultra Pure LLC, American Barrel Trust, Distillers Way LLC, L'eau Brune LLC, Provision Spirits LLC, KWH Venture LLC, Constellation Brands\n4. Add advanced search functionality with filters for mash bill patterns (75-21-00-04, 78-10-00-12, 60-36-00-04, etc.)\n5. Implement advanced filtering by ingredients, parameters, whiskey types, and customer\n6. Create recipe comparison tools for similar recipes\n7. Add template selection for new recipes with mash bill pattern recognition and template suggestions\n8. Implement import/export functionality for recipe data\n9. Create recipe duplication capability\n10. Add favorites and recently used functionality\n11. Implement template tagging system for quick discovery\n12. Develop revision-based template history and comparison\n13. Create template categorization by customer, product type, and complexity",
      "testStrategy": "1. Test template creation, storage, and retrieval\n2. Verify customer-specific organization and access control\n3. Test advanced search functionality with various mash bill patterns\n4. Validate filtering by whiskey types, ingredients, and other parameters\n5. Test recipe comparison tools with similar recipes\n6. Verify template suggestion functionality based on mash bill patterns\n7. Test import/export functionality for recipe data\n8. Validate template revision history and comparison features\n9. Test template categorization by customer, product type, and complexity\n10. Verify template tagging system functionality",
      "subtasks": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "title": "Design and Implement Recipe Template Data Model",
          "description": "Develop a relational data model to store whiskey recipe templates, supporting complex mash bill patterns, ingredients, parameters, and metadata for categorization and customer association.",
          "dependencies": [],
          "details": "Define tables/entities for recipes, ingredients, mash bill patterns, whiskey types, customers, and template metadata. Ensure the model supports extensibility for future features such as revision history and tagging.\n<info added on 2025-05-27T04:17:20.097Z>\nImplementing Recipe Template Data Model with TypeScript interfaces and data structures:\n\n```typescript\n// Core Template Interfaces\ninterface RecipeTemplate {\n  id: string;\n  name: string;\n  description: string;\n  createdAt: Date;\n  updatedAt: Date;\n  createdBy: string;\n  customerId?: string;\n  whiskeyTypeId: string;\n  complexity: ComplexityLevel;\n  tags: Tag[];\n  mashBill: MashBillComponent[];\n  isPublic: boolean;\n  revisions: TemplateRevision[];\n}\n\ninterface MashBillComponent {\n  ingredientId: string;\n  percentage: number;\n  order: number;\n}\n\ninterface Tag {\n  id: string;\n  name: string;\n  category: TagCategory;\n}\n\n// Supporting Types\nenum ComplexityLevel {\n  BEGINNER = 'beginner',\n  INTERMEDIATE = 'intermediate',\n  ADVANCED = 'advanced'\n}\n\nenum TagCategory {\n  FLAVOR_PROFILE = 'flavor_profile',\n  PRODUCTION_METHOD = 'production_method',\n  SPECIAL_TECHNIQUE = 'special_technique',\n  CUSTOMER_SPECIFIC = 'customer_specific'\n}\n\ninterface TemplateRevision {\n  id: string;\n  templateId: string;\n  version: number;\n  changes: string;\n  createdAt: Date;\n  createdBy: string;\n  snapshot: RecipeTemplate;\n}\n\n// Search and Filter Types\ninterface TemplateSearchParams {\n  query?: string;\n  whiskeyTypes?: string[];\n  tags?: string[];\n  complexity?: ComplexityLevel[];\n  customerId?: string;\n  createdBy?: string;\n  dateRange?: DateRange;\n}\n\ninterface DateRange {\n  startDate?: Date;\n  endDate?: Date;\n}\n\n// Utility type for mash bill pattern recognition\ninterface MashBillPattern {\n  pattern: string; // e.g. \"75-21-00-04\"\n  ingredients: {\n    corn?: number;\n    rye?: number;\n    wheat?: number;\n    malted_barley?: number;\n    other?: number;\n  }\n}\n```\n</info added on 2025-05-27T04:17:20.097Z>",
          "status": "done",
          "testStrategy": "Validate data integrity through unit tests and ensure the model supports all required relationships and constraints."
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "title": "Develop Template Categorization and Tagging System",
          "description": "Implement advanced categorization by whiskey type, customer, product type, complexity, and tagging for quick discovery and filtering.",
          "dependencies": [
            1
          ],
          "details": "Enable templates to be categorized and tagged dynamically, supporting multi-dimensional filtering and organization for diverse customer requirements.\n<info added on 2025-05-27T04:18:38.241Z>\nImplementation progress for Template Categorization and Tagging System:\n\n- Developed utility functions for mash bill pattern parsing and recognition to automatically identify and classify recipe templates\n- Implemented categorization logic that organizes templates by whiskey type, customer specifications, and production complexity\n- Created dynamic tagging system with metadata extraction for efficient template discovery\n- Built template validation functions to ensure data integrity and consistency\n- Established helper functions supporting advanced filtering capabilities including multi-dimensional search criteria\n- Designed utility architecture to support the upcoming template library search functionality in a scalable manner\n\nAll implementations follow the data model established in subtask 8.1 and are designed to integrate with the access control system planned in 8.3.\n</info added on 2025-05-27T04:18:38.241Z>",
          "status": "done",
          "testStrategy": "Test categorization and tagging through UI and API, ensuring templates can be filtered and discovered as expected."
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "title": "Implement Customer-Specific Access Control and Organization",
          "description": "Build access control mechanisms and organizational structures to ensure customers can only view, manage, and duplicate their own templates, supporting multiple organizations.",
          "dependencies": [
            1
          ],
          "details": "Integrate authentication and authorization layers, and structure template storage to enforce customer-specific visibility and management.\n<info added on 2025-05-27T04:20:21.980Z>\nImplementing Customer-Specific Access Control and Organization by:\n\n1. Developing access control functions that enforce template visibility boundaries between customers\n2. Structuring template storage with customer isolation to prevent unauthorized access\n3. Creating permission checking utilities for template view/edit/duplicate/share operations\n4. Implementing customer-specific template filtering and organizational structures\n5. Integrating with the existing authentication system to maintain customer context\n\nThis access control layer will ensure proper template isolation while supporting both customer-private templates and public template access with appropriate permission management.\n</info added on 2025-05-27T04:20:21.980Z>",
          "status": "done",
          "testStrategy": "Perform security and functional tests to verify access restrictions and correct template organization per customer."
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "title": "Develop Advanced Search and Filtering Functionality",
          "description": "Create robust search and filtering tools for templates, supporting queries by mash bill patterns, ingredients, parameters, whiskey types, tags, and customer.",
          "dependencies": [
            2,
            3
          ],
          "details": "Implement full-text and faceted search capabilities, allowing users to combine multiple filters and quickly locate relevant templates.\n<info added on 2025-05-27T04:21:32.010Z>\nImplementation of Advanced Search and Filtering Functionality is underway. Building on the established data model, utilities, and access control framework, the following components are being developed:\n\n1. Advanced search interface supporting multiple simultaneous filter criteria\n2. Real-time search functionality with debouncing and performance optimization techniques\n3. Faceted search capabilities with dynamic filter counts that update based on current result set\n4. Search result highlighting and relevance scoring to improve user experience\n5. Saved search functionality and search history tracking for user convenience\n6. Integration with mash bill pattern recognition algorithms for intelligent template matching\n\nAll search UI components are being designed to provide powerful discovery capabilities while maintaining strict adherence to customer-specific access controls established in previous phases.\n</info added on 2025-05-27T04:21:32.010Z>",
          "status": "done",
          "testStrategy": "Test search accuracy, filter combinations, and performance with a variety of real and synthetic data sets."
        },
