    {
      "id": 23,
      "title": "Implement Advanced Security Features",
      "description": "Add advanced security features including input validation, data encryption, and security auditing.",
      "details": "1. Implement comprehensive input validation and sanitization\n2. Add data encryption for sensitive information\n3. Create security headers configuration\n4. Implement Content Security Policy (CSP)\n5. Add protection against common web vulnerabilities (XSS, CSRF)\n6. Create security audit logging\n7. Implement session management with secure cookies\n8. Add rate limiting for sensitive operations\n9. Create security incident reporting mechanism",
      "testStrategy": "Test input validation with malicious payloads. Verify encryption of sensitive data. Test CSP implementation. Validate protection against common attack vectors. Test audit logging for security events.",
      "priority": "high",
      "dependencies": [
        3
      ],
      "status": "in-progress",
      "subtasks": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "title": "Implement Manufacturing-Specific Input Validation",
          "description": "Create comprehensive input validation for manufacturing-specific data including recipe codes, batch numbers, and proof values.",
          "dependencies": [],
          "details": "Develop validation rules for manufacturing data formats, implement sanitization for all user inputs, create specialized validators for distillery-specific values like proof percentages and aging parameters, and establish error handling for invalid inputs.\n<info added on 2025-05-25T02:34:08.459Z>\n# Manufacturing-Specific Input Validation Implementation\n\n## COMPLETED FEATURES:\n\n### Core Validation Library (/lib/validation.ts):\n1. **Zod Schema Validation** - Manufacturing-specific schemas for all whiskey production data types\n2. **Recipe Code Validation** - Format: XXX-##-##-##-##-R## (e.g., DWL-75-21-04-00-R01)\n3. **Batch ID Validation** - Format: BATCH-YYYY-MM-DD-### (e.g., BATCH-2025-05-25-001)\n4. **Proof Value Validation** - 0-200% ABV with 1 decimal place precision\n5. **Mash Bill Validation** - Format: ##-##-##-## with components totaling 100%\n6. **Manufacturing Parameter Validation** - Temperature (-20°F to 250°F), barrel quantities (1-1000), pH values (0-14), etc.\n7. **Production Status & Type Enums** - Bourbon types, container types, production statuses\n8. **Input Sanitization Classes** - DOMPurify-based XSS protection and character filtering\n9. **Comprehensive Error Handling** - Detailed validation errors with field-specific feedback\n\n### React Validation Components (/components/ui/manufacturing-input-validation.tsx):\n1. **ValidationField Component** - Real-time validation with visual feedback (green/red borders, icons)\n2. **ManufacturingInputValidationDemo** - Full interactive demonstration with 3 tabs\n3. **Production Data Tab** - Recipe codes, batch IDs, mash bills, proof values\n4. **Process Parameters Tab** - Temperature and barrel quantity inputs with ranges\n5. **Security Testing Tab** - XSS protection demonstration with malicious input testing\n6. **Sample Data Integration** - Realistic whiskey production data examples\n7. **Overall Form Validation** - Comprehensive validation with error aggregation\n\n### Demo Page (/app/security-demo/page.tsx):\n1. **Security Overview** - Complete implementation status and feature breakdown\n2. **Interactive Demo Integration** - Full validation system demonstration\n3. **Implementation Notes** - Technical details, regex patterns, and security libraries\n4. **Upcoming Features Preview** - Task 23.2-23.8 roadmap\n\n## SECURITY FEATURES IMPLEMENTED:\n- **XSS Protection**: DOMPurify sanitization removes malicious HTML/JavaScript\n- **Input Validation**: Manufacturing-specific format enforcement\n- **Real-time Feedback**: Immediate validation with visual indicators\n- **Character Filtering**: Removes unsafe characters while preserving valid input\n- **Business Rule Validation**: Mash bill percentages must total 100%, proper ranges for all manufacturing parameters\n\n## TECHNICAL ACHIEVEMENTS:\n- Fixed TypeScript exactOptionalPropertyTypes errors\n- Proper type safety throughout validation system\n- Manufacturing-appropriate error messages and examples\n- Interactive testing interface for security verification\n- Comprehensive regex patterns for whiskey industry standards\n</info added on 2025-05-25T02:34:08.459Z>",
          "status": "done",
          "testStrategy": "Test with valid and invalid manufacturing data samples, including boundary values for proof percentages and extreme batch number formats."
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "title": "Implement Production Data Encryption",
          "description": "Add encryption for sensitive production data including proprietary recipes, batch formulations, and quality control metrics.",
          "dependencies": [],
          "details": "Select appropriate encryption algorithms for production data, implement at-rest encryption for recipe databases, create secure key management for production environments, and ensure encrypted data transfer between production systems.\n<info added on 2025-05-25T03:23:21.440Z>\nImplementation of encryption for production data has been completed successfully with the following components:\n\nAES-256-CBC encryption system implemented in lib/security/encryption.ts with support for multiple data classification levels (Public, Internal, Confidential, Proprietary, Regulated) and manufacturing-specific data types (Recipe Formulation, Batch Parameters, Quality Metrics, Production Yields, Cost Data, Customer Specifications, Compliance Data).\n\nSecurity features include:\n- PBKDF2 key derivation with 100,000 iterations\n- HMAC authentication for data integrity\n- Key rotation capabilities for security compliance\n- Expiration support for temporary data encryption\n- Type-safe interfaces for RecipeData, BatchData, and QualityData\n- Utility functions for common encryption/decryption operations\n- Data classification enforcement for different sensitivity levels\n- Environment-specific master key support\n- Memory-safe operations with proper cleanup\n- Manufacturing data format validation\n- Audit trail with encryption metadata\n\nDemo components created:\n- Production data encryption demo component\n- Encryption test card with interactive testing capabilities\n- Updated security demo page with comprehensive encryption showcase\n\nThe system is production-ready and provides enterprise-grade security for sensitive whiskey production data including proprietary recipes, batch parameters, and regulatory compliance information.\n</info added on 2025-05-25T03:23:21.440Z>",
          "status": "done",
          "testStrategy": "Verify encrypted data cannot be read without proper authorization, test key rotation procedures, and validate encryption performance under production loads."
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "title": "Configure Factory Floor Display Security",
          "description": "Implement Content Security Policy (CSP) specifically for factory floor displays and control systems.",
