    {
      "id": 27,
      "title": "Implement Production Order Creation Wizard",
      "description": "Create a multi-step wizard interface for creating production orders with recipe selection, basic info/parameters, BOM configuration, and tank configuration steps, integrated with the existing production scheduling interface.",
      "details": "1. Extend the existing three-step Production Order Creation Wizard from Task 9 to a more comprehensive multi-step wizard with the following steps:\n\n   a. Recipe Selection:\n      - Implement a searchable and filterable recipe catalog\n      - Display recipe details including process parameters, expected yield, and quality metrics\n      - Add preview functionality to show recipe components and process flow\n      - Include version control indicators for recipes\n\n   b. Basic Information & Parameters:\n      - Create form fields for order name, batch ID, production date, quantity, priority\n      - Implement dynamic form validation using React Hook Form and Zod\n      - Add conditional fields based on recipe type selected\n      - Include production notes and special instructions fields\n\n   c. Bill of Materials (BOM) Configuration:\n      - Display the default BOM from the selected recipe\n      - Allow quantity adjustments with validation against inventory\n      - Implement material substitution functionality with compatibility checks\n      - Add lot/batch selection for raw materials with expiration date warnings\n      - Include cost calculation and variance from standard\n\n   d. Tank/Equipment Configuration:\n      - Create an interactive tank/equipment selection interface\n      - Implement availability checking against the production schedule\n      - Add capacity validation based on batch size\n      - Include cleaning status indicators and CIP scheduling\n      - Implement equipment-specific parameter configuration\n\n2. Integration Components:\n   - Connect wizard to the production scheduling interface from Task 9\n   - Implement state persistence between wizard steps using Zustand\n   - Create data validation at each step with clear error messaging\n   - Add a summary review step before final submission\n   - Implement draft saving functionality for incomplete orders\n\n3. UX Enhancements:\n   - Add progress indicator showing all steps and current position\n   - Implement keyboard navigation and shortcuts\n   - Create responsive design for all device sizes\n   - Add contextual help tooltips for complex fields\n   - Implement confirmation dialogs for potentially destructive actions\n\n4. Backend Integration:\n   - Connect to API endpoints for recipe data, inventory, equipment availability\n   - Implement real-time validation of selections against current system state\n   - Create proper error handling for API failures\n   - Add optimistic updates with rollback capability\n   - Implement WebSocket updates for collaborative editing\n\n5. Performance Considerations:\n   - Implement lazy loading of wizard steps\n   - Add caching for recipe and equipment data\n   - Optimize form rendering to prevent unnecessary re-renders\n   - Implement debounced validation for resource-intensive checks",
      "testStrategy": "1. Unit Testing:\n   - Write Jest tests for all wizard components\n   - Test form validation logic for each step\n   - Verify state management between steps\n   - Test conditional rendering based on user selections\n   - Validate error handling for API failures\n\n2. Integration Testing:\n   - Test the complete wizard flow from start to finish\n   - Verify data persistence between steps\n   - Test integration with the production scheduling interface\n   - Validate that created orders appear correctly in the schedule\n   - Test draft saving and resuming functionality\n\n3. User Acceptance Testing:\n   - Create test scenarios covering different recipe types\n   - Test with production planners to validate workflow efficiency\n   - Verify that all required production information is captured\n   - Test edge cases like large BOMs and complex equipment configurations\n   - Validate that the wizard handles real-world production scenarios\n\n4. Performance Testing:\n   - Measure load times for each wizard step\n   - Test with large datasets (many recipes, extensive BOMs)\n   - Verify responsive behavior on different devices\n   - Test concurrent usage scenarios\n\n5. Accessibility Testing:\n   - Verify keyboard navigation throughout the wizard\n   - Test screen reader compatibility\n   - Check color contrast and text readability\n   - Validate that error messages are properly announced\n\n6. Cross-browser Testing:\n   - Test on Chrome, Firefox, Safari, and Edge\n   - Verify mobile functionality on iOS and Android devices\n\n7. Regression Testing:\n   - Verify that existing production scheduling functionality works correctly\n   - Test that other parts of the system are not affected by the new wizard",
      "status": "done",
      "dependencies": [
